-- **Centralized Integration Hub**: All inbound and outbound traffic MUST pass through a dedicated Integration Gateway/Service. Internal microservices (like HRM or Document) are **FORBIDDEN** from calling external APIs directly.
+- **Centralized Integration Boundary**: Route external-system traffic through the approved integration boundary and a server-controlled destination registry. Do not accept arbitrary upstream URLs; validate scheme, host/address, DNS/redirect behavior, method/path, timeout, size, and record count.
@@
-- **Integration Audit Log**: EVERY cross-system integration call must be logged in an `IntegrationLog` table. This log must capture: `TransactionId`, `ExternalEndpoint`, `Direction` (Inbound/Outbound), `Payload` (Masked for sensitive info), `ResponseStatus`, and `Timestamp`.
+- **Integration Audit Log**: Record transaction/correlation ID, registered destination identifier, direction, operation, result/status, duration, timestamp, and an approved hash or masked summary. Store full payload only when classification, purpose, access, encryption, and retention are explicitly approved.
+- **Credential Isolation**: Use server-side `secretRef` material. Never forward browser cookies, Hub tokens, arbitrary identity headers, or upstream `Set-Cookie` across trust boundaries.
